ents":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6147788455","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/86#issuecomment-6147788455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/86","id":6147788455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbm_Opw","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T14:24:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T14:24:48Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — MEDIUM — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **HIGH · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Inbound RDP (TCP/3389) permitted from external source address**\n  - Category rationale: The NSG permits inbound RDP (TCP/3389) from an external source address (203.0.113.10/32) at priority 301, which takes precedence over the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096. This is a concrete, evidence-supported inbound access weakness: RDP is a high-value attack surface and exposing it from any external address, even a single IP, represents a real vulnerability. The comment 'Deliberately unrestricted RDP access' confirms the rule is intentional but does not eliminate the security risk.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowRDP': direction = 'Inbound', access = 'Allow', protocol = 'Tcp', destination_port_range = '3389', source_address_prefix = '203.0.113.10/32', priority = 301. The DenyAllInbound rule is at priority 4096 and does not block this traffic.\n  - Analysis: The security_rule 'AllowRDP' in azurerm_network_security_group.nsg allows inbound TCP traffic on port 3389 from source address 203.0.113.10/32 to any destination, at priority 301. This rule takes precedence over the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096. The comment acknowledges this as 'deliberately unrestricted RDP access for controlled security testing only', but the rule as configured permits external RDP sessions to any resource in the associated subnet. 203.0.113.0/24 is a TEST-NET-3 address per RFC 5737, which may indicate a placeholder; if deployed with this or a real external IP, inbound RDP is exposed. RDP has a significant vulnerability history and should not be directly accessible from external addresses in any environment without strong compensating controls (e.g., MFA, JIT access, bastion host).\n  - Impact: Any host at the source address (or a real external IP if 203.0.113.10/32 is a placeholder) can attempt RDP connections to all resources in the associated subnet. RDP brute-force, credential stuffing, and exploitation of RDP vulnerabilities (e.g., BlueKeep-class) are realistic attack vectors. A compromised RDP session would provide direct interactive access to subnet resources.\n  - Recommendation: Remove or disable the AllowRDP rule unless RDP access is operationally required for the test case and documented with approval. If RDP testing is required, restrict access further via Azure Bastion, Just-In-Time VM Access (Microsoft Defender for Cloud), or a dedicated VPN/jump host rather than a direct NSG allow rule. Confirm that 203.0.113.10/32 is not a placeholder and that the source IP is tightly controlled. Document the approval and time-bound nature of the rule in the PR and in the NSG rule description field.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6147788455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/user